# Slice 307 (CALL-WHOLE-ARGUMENTS-STRUCTURE), the author's answer and order of 2026-11-08 through Codex (LMX_blog/2026-11-08.md): a
# call with one Structure argument whose direct fields name the formals is the call with those fields as its arguments -- the basic
# rule, whatever else the Structure might fit, in native and in the interpreter.  k (Q: q; int: z 0) given QZ (int: z 5; Q: q) with
# QZ\q\z built as 1: q <- QZ\q and z <- QZ\z, no default -- k records what it received (Seen: q\z 1, z 5; the default 0 would give
# 10) and reads q\z * 10 + z = 15; nothing is searched for deeper in QZ, and that QZ would also fit the formal q as a value is not a
# question the rule asks (the first pass refused this call as ambiguous and the second held it: both my own additions, withdrawn).
# The explicit supply k(q: QZ) is the other spelling: q <- QZ (q\z then reads QZ\z = 5), z its default 0, 50.  Entry 7; 80.. the
# failing check.
Q:
    int: z 1
end: Q
QZ:
    int: z 5
    Q: q
end: QZ
Seen:
    int: qz 0
    int: z 0
    int: n 0
end: Seen
fn: k (Q: q; int: z 0) int
    Seen\n: Seen\n + 1
    Seen\qz: q\z
    Seen\z: z
    return: q\z * 10 + z
end: k
fn: direct () int
    return: k(QZ)
end: direct
fn: named () int
    return: k(q: QZ)
end: named
fn: run () int
    QZ\q\z: 1
    if: direct() != 15
        return: 80
    if: Seen\qz != 1
        return: 81
    if: Seen\z != 5
        return: 82
    if: named() != 50
        return: 83
    if: Seen\qz != 5 || Seen\z != 0
        return: 84
    if: Seen\n != 2
        return: 85
    return: 7
end: run
int: code run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
